INT. DEEP-SPACE SURVEY SHIP - BRIDGE - SHIP NIGHT

A cramped circular chamber ringed by consoles. A long viewport shows a field of unfamiliar stars. Red alert lights wash the faces of six sleepless people.

CAPTAIN MARGUERITE ADEOLA, 50s, stands at the centre console, a coffee gone cold in her hand. She keeps her eyes on the screen.

COMMANDER SOREN VASQUEZ, 40s, at navigation, hunches over a plot, fingers drumming.

DR. LILIANA PETROV, 30s, the ship's medic, at the aft hatch, a first-aid kit at her hip. She has not slept in two days.

ENSIGN BASHIR KOROMA, 20s, at comms, fidgets with a headset. He is very pale.

TECHNICIAN ODALYS GRAU, 30s, at engineering, wipes grease from her hands with a rag and says nothing.

CHIEF IVO TEMBO, 60s, in the corner, arms crossed, scowls at everyone and everything.

A bang from below. The deck shudders. She grips the rail. He staggers. They all look up.

ADEOLA
Report!

VASQUEZ
Hull breach on deck four.

PETROV
Is anyone down there?

TEMBO
Not anymore.

Petrov crosses herself. Koroma stifles a whimper.

GRAU
Reactor holding at sixty percent.

ADEOLA
Can we make the jump?

GRAU
In nine minutes. If nobody breathes on it.

ADEOLA
Everyone, hold your breath.

A laugh, thin and nervous. Koroma wipes his eyes. The deck shudders again, but gently this time, as if the ship were exhaling.

VASQUEZ
Captain. Coordinates locked.

ADEOLA
Execute.

The stars in the viewport smear to white lines. The red alert dims to amber. She sets the coffee on the rail and rests her forehead against the cold glass.
